# Pin LF in the repository AND in the working tree, for two concrete reasons.
#
# 1. The Makefile and scripts/*.sh run inside the Linux container. A CRLF
#    checkout makes the kernel read the shebang as "/bin/bash\r" and fail with
#    "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — an error that names the
#    interpreter, never the line ending.
#
# 2. workflows/*.json carries the indexer's jsCode, which measures chunk length
#    in characters. A CRLF blob is one byte per line longer than the LF blob the
#    GitHub API serves, which is enough to move a note across the 1500-char
#    boundary and silently change the index.
#
# `text=auto` keeps binary detection, so an image added later is left alone
# without editing this file.
* text=auto eol=lf
